---
title: Design class diagram 6 of 8 - API controllers, part 2 (Strategies.Api/Controllers)
---
classDiagram
    direction LR

    class DocumentsController {
        <<controller api/documents>>
        -_context: ApplicationDbContext
        +GetDocuments(caseId: Guid?, page: int = 1, pageSize: int = 20) Task~IActionResult~
        +GetDocument(id: Guid) Task~IActionResult~
        +DownloadDocument(id: Guid) Task~IActionResult~
        +UploadDocument(file: IFormFile) Task~IActionResult~
        +CreateDocument(dto: CreateDocumentRequest) Task~IActionResult~
        +UpdateDocumentStatus(id: Guid, dto: UpdateDocumentStatusRequest) Task~IActionResult~
        +ArchiveDocument(id: Guid) Task~IActionResult~
    }
    class AdminController {
        <<controller api/admin>>
        -_context: ApplicationDbContext
        +GetUsers(page: int = 1, pageSize: int = 10, search: string?) Task~IActionResult~
        +SuspendUser(id: Guid) Task~IActionResult~
        +ReinstateUser(id: Guid) Task~IActionResult~
        +DeleteUser(id: Guid) Task~IActionResult~
        +GetAuditLogs(page: int = 1, pageSize: int = 20, userId: Guid?) Task~IActionResult~
    }
    class StatsController {
        <<controller api/stats>>
        -_context: ApplicationDbContext
        +GetAdminStats() Task~IActionResult~
        +GetConsultantStats() Task~IActionResult~
        +GetClientStats(clientId: Guid) Task~IActionResult~
    }
    class NotificationController {
        <<controller api/notifications>>
        -_context: ApplicationDbContext
        +GetNotifications(page: int = 1, pageSize: int = 20) Task~IActionResult~
        +MarkAsRead(id: Guid) Task~IActionResult~
    }
    class DocumentTypesController {
        <<controller api/DocumentTypes>>
        -_context: ApplicationDbContext
        +GetDocumentTypes() Task~IActionResult~
    }
    class ApplicationDbContext {
        <<DbContext, see diagram 8>>
    }

    DocumentsController --> ApplicationDbContext
    AdminController --> ApplicationDbContext
    StatsController --> ApplicationDbContext
    NotificationController --> ApplicationDbContext
    DocumentTypesController --> ApplicationDbContext

    note "All five extend ControllerBase, require a signed-in user and<br>query ApplicationDbContext directly (no service layer).<br>Optional parameters default to null. Access rules:<br>DocumentsController: Upload, Create any role; UpdateDocumentStatus,<br>ArchiveDocument Admin or Consultant; case ownership is checked.<br>AdminController: Admin only. DeleteUser is a soft delete<br>(IsActive = false, the same state as SuspendUser).<br>StatsController: GetAdminStats Admin; GetConsultantStats<br>Admin or Consultant; GetClientStats any role."
